<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Early Duchy of Aquitaine</h1><p class="st-meta">660 CE – 769 CE (approx.) · capital Toulouse</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Independent duchy of south-western Gaul whose dukes defied the Franks and fought the Umayyad advance in the 8th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As Merovingian power weakened in the mid 7th century, the region south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> came under semi-independent dukes. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/felix-of-aquitaine">Felix</a>, a nobleman of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-toulouse">Toulouse</a>, is recorded around 660, followed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lupus-i-of-aquitaine">Lupus</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odo-the-great">Odo</a>, called the Great, who ruled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-aquitaine">Aquitaine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a> from around 700.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The duchy kept a strong Gallo-Roman identity and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odo-the-great">Odo</a> defeated an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad</a> army besieging <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-toulouse">Toulouse</a> in 721, one of the first checks on the Muslim advance, but was routed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bordeaux">Bordeaux</a> in 732 and had to seek help from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a>, joining him at the battle near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odo-the-great">Odo</a>'s son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hunald-i-of-aquitaine">Hunald</a> and grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waiofar">Waiofar</a> resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingians</a>, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short">Pippin the Short</a> waged yearly wars against Waiofar until his murder in 768. A last rising under a second Hunald was crushed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> in 769, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-aquitaine">Aquitaine</a> became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-franks">Kingdom of the Franks</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="duchy, 660 CE – 769 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">duchy</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:72.84%;width:2.17%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>660 CE – 769 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Toulouse</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Odo the Great, Hunald, Waiofar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin, Old Occitan</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Odonid Aquitaine</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=714&amp;focus=early-duchy-of-aquitaine" aria-label="Early Duchy of Aquitaine on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4715 632 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Early Duchy of Aquitaine lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5035 888L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5035 888h0"/><path class="ma